{
  "$comment": [
    "Reference cases for the astrology engine.",
    "",
    "Two kinds of entries, and the difference matters:",
    "  * verified_independently = true  -> the expected value comes from an",
    "    outside authority (NASA/JPL eclipse catalogue, published equinox and",
    "    solstice times, published retrograde windows). These are real",
    "    regression tests.",
    "  * verified_independently = false -> the expected value was produced by",
    "    *this* engine and only sanity-checked. They guard against accidental",
    "    change, but they are NOT evidence of correctness; comparing them with",
    "    a second, independent calculator is a pre-launch task. Do not promote",
    "    an entry to true without recording where the value came from.",
    "",
    "Angles are degrees, instants are UTC ISO-8601, tolerances are in the unit",
    "of the quantity being compared."
  ],
